* ============================================================
*  PINOCCHIO INDEX MCC DIMS -- CDX + LMDB for the newly converted
*  MCC dimension tables (2026-09-23, owner: "I just added the rest
*  of the MCC tables to pinocchio and converted them to x64").
*
*  Status:  CANDIDATE / REVIEW_BEFORE_EXECUTION. INDEX-ONLY: no table
*           is created, imported, erased, or written -- this script
*           adds CDX containers + LMDB envs beside EXISTING tables.
*           The fact fixtures (STUDENTS 1M, ENROLL 5.5M) and the
*           already-indexed dims (CLASSES, MAJORS from
*           pinocchio_build_dims.dts) are NOT opened.
*  Tags:    FIELD KEYS ONLY, per the corrected contract of 2026-07-14
*           (CONTRACT_DRIFT_INDEX_EXPRESSION_2026-07-14.md). The two
*           FoxPro expression tags in the MCC provenance notes (NAME,
*           TCSEC) are NOT buildable and are deliberately absent.
*  Tag set: TEACHERS TID, DEPT_ID; COURSES CID, DEPT_ID; DEPT DEPT_ID;
*           ROOMS ROOM; TERMS TERM; STUD_MAJ SID; TASSIGN CLS_ID.
*           BUILDING: no tags defined in the schema contract -- skipped
*           on purpose, not forgotten.
*  Recipe:  the pinocchio_build_dims.dts idiom exactly: USE, CDX
*           CREATE, CDX ADDTAG <field>, BUILDLMDB TINY CLEAN YES,
*           CDX TAGS, then the tag-sanity gate (COUNT under the tag
*           must equal physical COUNT -- the first-run lesson).
*           ADDTAG refuses a name that is not a field, so a schema
*           mismatch fails loudly here rather than silently at BUILD.
*  Safety:  CDX CREATE refuses an existing container, so a rerun over
*           an already-indexed table stops at the refusal and mutates
*           nothing. To rebuild, erase the container first by hand.
*  Outputs: indexes/pinocchio/<t>.cdx (+ .meta)   <- commit these
*           lmdb/pinocchio/<t>.cdx.d/             <- derived, gitignored
* ============================================================
SET ECHO OFF
SET TIMER ON

SET PATH DBF DBF/pinocchio
SET PATH INDEXES INDEXES/pinocchio
SET PATH LMDB LMDB/pinocchio
CLOSE

ECHO === TEACHERS: expect ~20 rows; tags TID, DEPT_ID ===
USE TEACHERS
COUNT
CDX CREATE
CDX ADDTAG TID
CDX ADDTAG DEPT_ID
BUILDLMDB TINY CLEAN YES
CDX TAGS
SET ORDER TO TAG TID
COUNT
SET ORDER TO PHYSICAL
CLOSE

ECHO === COURSES: expect ~100 rows; tags CID, DEPT_ID ===
USE COURSES
COUNT
CDX CREATE
CDX ADDTAG CID
CDX ADDTAG DEPT_ID
BUILDLMDB TINY CLEAN YES
CDX TAGS
SET ORDER TO TAG CID
COUNT
SET ORDER TO PHYSICAL
CLOSE

ECHO === DEPT: expect ~10 rows; tag DEPT_ID ===
USE DEPT
COUNT
CDX CREATE
CDX ADDTAG DEPT_ID
BUILDLMDB TINY CLEAN YES
CDX TAGS
SET ORDER TO TAG DEPT_ID
COUNT
SET ORDER TO PHYSICAL
CLOSE

ECHO === ROOMS: expect ~30 rows; tag ROOM ===
USE ROOMS
COUNT
CDX CREATE
CDX ADDTAG ROOM
BUILDLMDB TINY CLEAN YES
CDX TAGS
SET ORDER TO TAG ROOM
COUNT
SET ORDER TO PHYSICAL
CLOSE

ECHO === TERMS: expect ~3 rows; tag TERM ===
USE TERMS
COUNT
CDX CREATE
CDX ADDTAG TERM
BUILDLMDB TINY CLEAN YES
CDX TAGS
SET ORDER TO TAG TERM
COUNT
SET ORDER TO PHYSICAL
CLOSE

ECHO === STUD_MAJ: expect ~200 rows; tag SID ===
USE STUD_MAJ
COUNT
CDX CREATE
CDX ADDTAG SID
BUILDLMDB TINY CLEAN YES
CDX TAGS
SET ORDER TO TAG SID
COUNT
SET ORDER TO PHYSICAL
CLOSE

ECHO === TASSIGN: expect ~200 rows; tag CLS_ID ===
USE TASSIGN
COUNT
CDX CREATE
CDX ADDTAG CLS_ID
BUILDLMDB TINY CLEAN YES
CDX TAGS
SET ORDER TO TAG CLS_ID
COUNT
SET ORDER TO PHYSICAL
CLOSE

ECHO === BUILDING: skipped by contract (no tags defined) ===

ECHO === DONE. Read rule: every table must open as (v64); every
ECHO === SET ORDER must print CDX TAG '<tag>' (ASC) -- a "file not
ECHO === found: ...cnx" line means the table is NOT x64, the flavor
ECHO === routing never reached the CDX, and the COUNT gate below is
ECHO === BLIND (both counts are physical and equal trivially).
ECHO === Measured 2026-09-23, first run: all seven dims opened (v32),
ECHO === every SET ORDER missed, and the gate passed without engaging
ECHO === -- the PKP_G5 shape. Then: COUNT twice EQUAL under a REAL
ECHO === tag attach; every BUILDLMDB OK; CDX TAGS exactly as added.
